Z||000000||cmyokley||10-13-1999||03:01 PM||||I have rebuilt the V6 in my 86GT and really have not driven it very hard untill recently. I am noticing that at RPM's over 4000 the motor is cutting out like the ignition is miss firing.<P>I have replaced everything possible including the distributor, plug wires, cap and plugs and have even upgraded the coil to an MSD ignition. <P>The car runs great and is very fast but should not be missing at 4000+RPM.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||10-13-1999||04:15 PM||||remove the tach filter. it may be on it's way south.<P>check the fuel system. it may be low pressure or not flowing enough volume. where the injectors replaced? If not did you have them flow tested.<P>check the distrubutor shaft for play. replace the pickup and module. I know you said you just replaced it, but it don't mean it's good.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-13-1999).]||||reg||1
